{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-40863","model_call":51,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ vit \"quality of life\" (+ venom bee wasp sting stings hymenoptera))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ vit \"quality of life\" (+ venom bee wasp sting stings hymenoptera))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1463836094#8_2825251705","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1083","rank":1,"snippet":"often positive than serum-specific IgE and correlate better with history. Baseline tryptase should be measured. Those with raised levels have a higher risk of severe systemic reactions. Treatment of patients with bee or wasp sting allergy All patients with a history of systemic reaction should be immediately provided with a written emergency management plan, an adrenaline (epinephrine) auto-injector and education in its use. With children, appropriate liaison with the school is recommended. Venom immunotherapy (VIT) is recommended for all patients with a severe systemic reaction after a sting. It reduces the chances of a serious allergic reaction to an insect <cover>sting and improves quality of life. VIT </cover>is the only specific treatment that is currently available for patients with a history of systemic reaction to a Hymenoptera insect sting. VIT is effective in 95% of patients allergic to wasp venom and about 80% of those allergic to bee venom. VIT is not often recommended for children.\" , \"start_char\": 4702.000000 , \"title\": \"Insect Bites and Stings Treatment Information | Patient\" , \"url\": \"https://patient.info/doctor/insect-bites-and-stings-pro\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1463836094#8_2825251705","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":47},"model_calls":51,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
