{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-40863","model_call":52,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1084"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1084"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1463836094#8_2825251705","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1084","rank":4,"snippet":"Stings Insect Bites and Stings This article is for Medical Professionals<cover>Hymenoptera stings Systemic reaction to wasp or bee stings Investigation of patients with bee or wasp sting allergy Treatment of patients with bee or wasp sting allergy Management of bee or wasp stings Blood-sucking flies True bugs (Hemiptera) Ticks (Ixodoidea) Management Harvest mites (Trombiculidae) Join our weekly wellness digest from the best health experts in the business \" , \"segment\": \"Skin tests are also more often positive than serum-specific IgE and correlate better with history. Baseline tryptase should be measured. Those with raised levels have a higher risk of severe systemic reactions. Treatment of patients with bee or wasp sting allergy All patients with a history of systemic reaction should be immediately provided with a written emergency management plan, an adrenaline (epinephrine) auto-injector and education in its use. With children, appropriate liaison with the school is recommended. Venom immunotherapy (VIT) is recommended for all patients with a severe systemic reaction after a sting. It reduces the chances of a serious allergic reaction to an insect sting and improves quality of life. </cover>VIT is the only specific treatment that is currently available for ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_25_1463836094#8_2825251705","rank":4,"relevance":3}]},"time":4},"model_calls":52,"document_judgments":31,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
