{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-40863","model_call":68,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1100"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1100"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1067819329#4_1802449718","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1100","rank":2,"snippet":"Information on Vaccine Vials Sample Adjustment to Immunotherapy Following Interruption of Dosage Schedule Potential Adverse Reactions to Allergy Vaccines and Suggested Treatment Checklist for Safe Vaccine Administration Safety Issues Equipment and Medications Needed to Treat Anaphylaxis View/Print Figure Assessment of Immunotherapy Efficacy The Authors REFERENCES Continue reading from August 15, 2004 \" , \"segment\": \"2 Since then, controlled studies have shown that allergen immunotherapy is effective in patients with allergic rhinitis, allergic conjunctivitis, allergic asthma, and allergic reactions to <cover>Hymenoptera venom. 3 – 6 Patients with one or more of these diagnoses are considered for immunotherapy if they have well-defined, clinically relevant allergic triggers that markedly affect their quality of life </cover>or daily function, and if they do not attain adequate symptom relief with avoidance measures and pharmacotherapy. Despite proven efficacy, the exact mechanism of allergen immunotherapy remains unknown. Selection of Patients To make a definitive diagnosis of allergy, IgE-mediated, type I, immediate-hypersensitivity skin testing typically is performed by scratching diluted allergen into the skin surface or by injecting it intradermally. A positive skin test reaction reflects the presence of specific IgE antibodies to the tested allergen, and a correlation of the specific ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1067819329#4_1802449718","rank":2,"relevance":2}]},"time":11},"model_calls":68,"document_judgments":36,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
