{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-40863","model_call":75,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"venom immunotherapy\" (+ anxiety fear) (+ bee wasp hymenoptera sting stings))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"venom immunotherapy\" (+ anxiety fear) (+ bee wasp hymenoptera sting stings))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#8_1823903949","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1107","rank":1,"snippet":"venom and bee envenoming therapy. Front Immunol. 2019;10:2090. What are the clinical features of bee and wasp stings? What are the complications of bee and wasp stings? How is bee and wasp sting allergy diagnosed? What is the differential diagnosis for bee and wasp stings? What is the treatment for bee and wasp stings? Prevention Treatment of localised site reactions Treatment for systemic reactions<cover>Venom immunotherapy desensitisation What is the outcome for bee and wasp stings? Related information Bibliography On DermNet NZ Other websites Skin cancer Dermatology Made Easy Book Call for sponsors Sign up to the newsletter \" , \"segment\": \"Blistering Secondary bacterial skin infection, including cellulitis and lymphangitis Persistent reaction lasting weeks or months Vasculitis, serum sickness, neurological effects Impact on quality of life — anxiety </cover>resulting in social restriction. Unusual reactions to bee and wasp stings Wasp sting reaction persisted for more than 6 weeks Wasp sting reaction causing localised vasculitis with purpura Blistering reaction to a bee sting How is bee and wasp sting allergy diagnosed? Both skin testing and serologic tests should be performed on patients with a history of a systemic reaction to a bee or wasp sting, and ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#8_1823903949","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":49},"model_calls":75,"document_judgments":37,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
