{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-40863","model_call":75,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1107"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1107"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_1274088377#14_2688362500","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1107","rank":2,"snippet":"How common are allergies? Symptoms and Causes What are the symptoms of allergies? What causes allergies? Diagnosis and Tests How are allergies diagnosed? Management and Treatment How are allergies treated? Outlook / Prognosis Can allergies be cured? Get useful, helpful and relevant health + wellness information \" , \"segment\": \"Swelling of your face, throat or mouth tissue. Wheezing or difficulty swallowing. Restlessness and <cover>anxiety. Rapid pulse. Dizziness or a sharp drop in your blood pressure. If you have a reaction like this, a re-sting can cause a serious reaction that can be life-threatening. An allergic reaction is treated with epinephrine (adrenaline). If you’ve had an allergic reaction to bee stings, see a board-certified allergy/immunologist to get a skin and/or blood test to confirm your allergy to bee venom. Venom immunotherapy </cover>is recommended if venom allergy is confirmed. This will help reduce the possibility that a re-sting will cause a serious reaction.\" , \"start_char\": 7002.000000 , \"title\": \"Allergies: Types, Symptoms, Causes & Treatments\" , \"url\": \"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/diseases/8610-allergy-overview\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_05_1004088852#8_1823903949","rank":1,"relevance":3}]},"time":10},"model_calls":75,"document_judgments":37,"relevance_3":8,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
